- **Ensure all interactive elements are keyboard accessible and screen reader compatible.**

## Accessibility Standards (ADA/WCAG Compliance)

### Core Requirements
- **Target WCAG 2.1 Level AA compliance as the minimum standard.**
- Implement semantic HTML5 elements for proper document structure.
- Ensure all functionality is available via keyboard navigation.
- Provide text alternatives for all non-text content.
- Maintain a minimum color contrast ratio of 4.5:1 for normal text and 3:1 for large text.
- Implement proper focus indicators and focus management.
- Use ARIA labels, roles, and properties appropriately (but prefer semantic HTML first).
- Ensure all forms have proper labels and error messaging.
- Implement skip navigation links for keyboard users.
- Test with screen readers (NVDA, JAWS, VoiceOver).

### Accessibility Implementation Guidelines
- **Forms & Inputs:**
  - Associate all form controls with labels using `for` attribute or wrapping.
  - Provide clear, descriptive error messages linked to form fields.
  - Use `aria-required`, `aria-invalid`, and `aria-describedby` attributes.
  - Group related form fields with `<fieldset>` and `<legend>`.
  - Implement proper autocomplete attributes.

- **Navigation & Interactive Elements:**
  - Ensure all interactive elements have visible focus indicators.
  - Implement logical tab order using `tabindex` when necessary.
  - Provide keyboard shortcuts documentation.
  - Use `role="navigation"` and proper ARIA landmarks.
  - Implement breadcrumb navigation with proper ARIA markup.

- **Content & Media:**
  - Provide alt text for all images (empty alt="" for decorative images).
  - Include captions and transcripts for videos.
  - Use proper heading hierarchy (h1-h6) without skipping levels.
  - Ensure sufficient color contrast for all text.
  - Avoid using color alone to convey information.

- **Dynamic Content & Livewire:**
  - Announce dynamic content changes using ARIA live regions.
  - Manage focus when content updates or modals open/close.
  - Provide loading states with appropriate ARIA attributes.
  - Ensure all Livewire components maintain accessibility after updates.

