## Code Examples for Common Accessibility Patterns

### Accessible Form Example
```blade
<form wire:submit.prevent="save" role="form" aria-label="User Registration">
    <div class="form-control">
        <label for="name" class="label">
            <span class="label-text">Name <span class="text-error" aria-label="required">*</span></span>
        </label>
        <input 
            type="text" 
            id="name"
            wire:model="name" 
            class="input input-bordered @error('name') input-error @enderror"
            aria-required="true"
            aria-invalid="@error('name') true @else false @enderror"
            aria-describedby="name-error"
        >
        @error('name')
            <span id="name-error" class="text-error text-sm mt-1" role="alert">{{ $message }}</span>
        @enderror
    </div>
</form>
```

### Accessible Modal Pattern
```blade
<div x-data="{ open: false }" 
     x-trap.noscroll="open"
     @keydown.escape.window="open = false">
    <button @click="open = true" aria-haspopup="dialog">Open Modal</button>
    
    <div x-show="open" 
         role="dialog" 
         aria-modal="true"
         aria-labelledby="modal-title"
         class="modal">
        <div class="modal-box">
            <h2 id="modal-title" class="text-lg font-bold">Modal Title</h2>
            <!-- Modal content -->
            <button @click="open = false" aria-label="Close modal">×</button>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
```

### Live Region for Dynamic Updates
```blade
<div wire:loading.delay aria-live="polite" aria-busy="true">
    <span class="sr-only">Loading...</span>
</div>

<div aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
    @if (session()->has('message'))
        <div role="alert">{{ session('message') }}</div>
    @endif
</div>
```

